<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Catamarca Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Catamarca is a province in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>, with its capital at San Fernando del Valle de Catamarca, founded in 1683. Andean ranges and dry valleys cover much of it, and it was home to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diaguita">Diaguita</a> peoples who resisted Spanish rule in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calchaqui-wars">Calchaquí Wars</a>. It was part of the short-lived Republic of Tucumán before becoming an autonomous province in 1821.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/catamarca-province.jpg" alt="Catamarca Province" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Camino a Campo de Piedra Pomez en Catamarca · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CATAMARCA_318_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
